{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:53:13.205772", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### **Network Health Overview**\\nThe network appears to have significant connectivity issues. The reachability test results indicate that most hosts are unable to communicate with critical infrastructure components such as the DNS server and other hosts. This suggests a widespread anomaly affecting host-to-host and host-to-server communication.\\n\\n#### **Findings**\\n1. **Host Reachability Issues**:\\n   - None of the hosts (e.g., `host_1_1_1_1`, `host_1_2_2_1`, etc.) are able to reach the DNS server (`10.200.0.2`) or other hosts in the network.\\n   - The status for all host-to-host and host-to-DNS communication is marked as \"unknown,\" indicating a failure in establishing connectivity.\\n\\n2. **Server Communication**:\\n   - Servers such as the DHCP server, load balancer, and web servers (`web_server_0`, `web_server_1`, etc.) successfully communicate with the DNS server (`10.200.0.2`) with no packet loss and low RTT values. This suggests that the server farm and its internal communication are functioning correctly.\\n\\n3. **Infrastructure Connectivity**:\\n   - The DHCP server (`10.200.0.8`) successfully communicates with the DNS server, indicating that the server access router and core routers are likely operational for server-to-server traffic.\\n   - The load balancer (`10.200.0.7`) and web servers (`10.200.0.3` to `10.200.0.6`) also have successful communication with the DNS server.\\n\\n4. **Host-to-Server Communication**:\\n   - Hosts are unable to reach the DNS server or other servers in the network. This could indicate issues with the distribution layer routers, access switches, or OSPF routing configuration.\\n\\n#### **Potential Root Causes**\\nBased on the findings, the following root causes are suspected:\\n1. **Access Layer Issues**:\\n   - The access switches may not be forwarding traffic correctly, leading to host isolation from the rest of the network.\\n\\n2. **Routing Problems**:\\n   - OSPF configuration issues in the distribution or core routers may be preventing proper route advertisement for host subnets.\\n\\n3. **DHCP Configuration**:\\n   - Hosts may not be receiving proper IP configuration via DHCP, resulting in communication failures.\\n\\n4. **Network Segmentation**:\\n   - VLAN misconfigurations or trunking issues between switches and routers could be causing traffic isolation.\\n\\n#### **Next Steps**\\nFurther investigation is required to pinpoint the exact cause of the anomaly. This includes:\\n- Verifying OSPF configurations on the routers.\\n- Checking VLAN and trunk configurations on the access switches.\\n- Inspecting DHCP relay functionality and host IP configurations.\\n- Analyzing traffic flow and packet drops at the access layer.\\n\\nThis concludes the initial diagnostic report., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='68c89d56-0fbf-4a1e-98ec-881ab2b878ee'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
